cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Mandarin-EmoStim: offline Mandarin speech emotion quantification with personalized auditory stimulus generation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Jiawei"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-10
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/lijiawei255/mandarin-emo-stim"
url: "https://github.com/lijiawei255/mandarin-emo-stim"
keywords:
  - speech emotion recognition
  - Mandarin
  - affective computing
  - Russell circumplex
  - auditory stimulus
abstract: >-
  A fully offline desktop research tool that quantifies the emotional state of
  Mandarin speech on Russell's valence-arousal plane by late fusion of six
  modalities (emotion2vec, prosody, paralinguistic events, physical acoustics,
  LLM text semantics, lexicon statistics) and generates differentiated auditory
  stimuli per quadrant. Evaluation on public corpora (AISHELL-3, CSEMOTIONS) is
  documented in docs/evaluation.md.
